# Selective synchronisation: sync ONLY the 'Code' folder from the OneDrive root.
# Everything else on OneDrive is excluded - 'sync_list' excludes everything by
# default and requires explicit inclusion.
#
# Stow-managed from ~/.dotfiles/onedrive - edit THIS file, not the live path
# (~/.config/onedrive/sync_list is a symlink to it).
#
# Rules are relative to sync_dir (i.e. the OneDrive root).
# A LEADING '/' anchors the rule to the OneDrive root. This matters: rules
# without a leading slash match ANYWHERE and force an exhaustive scan of the
# whole account (slow, heavy on the API).
#
# '/Code'     - the Code folder itself, in the root only
# '/Code/**'  - belt-and-braces recursive inclusion for everything beneath it
#
# Before the first real sync, validate what this will actually do:
#   onedrive --display-config                 # confirm sync_dir + sync_list are picked up
#   onedrive --sync --dry-run --verbose       # confirm ONLY /Code is in scope

/Code
/Code/**
